<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tē^trăchordos</span></b> ,
			on, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράχορδος, ον,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having four
			strings</i> or <i>notes.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">machina,</span>”
				<i>a water-organ</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					10, 13</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tē^trăchordon</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-dum</span></b> ), i,
			n., <i>a chord of four notes</i>, <i>a tetrachord.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart.
					Cap. 9</span></i>, §§ 935 and 941;
					<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 19 <i>med.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: anni, i. e. <i>the four
				seasons</i>, Varr ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 71,
			16</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
